.TH MARKPASTE 1 "2026-10-21" "Markpaste @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
markpaste \- capture, mark and paste screenshots with comments into any chat
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B markpaste
[\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B markpaste
runs in the background with a tray icon. A global hotkey captures a screen area;
numbered marks A1, A2\&... with comments are put on the shot in the editor.
Another hotkey pastes the whole set, images one by one and then the message text,
into the active chat window.
.PP
Started again while running, it passes the command to the running instance and exits.
This lets the commands below be bound to keys in desktops without global shortcuts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-\-capture
Capture with editor: select an area, then add marks and comments.
.TP
.B \-\-capture\-to\-strip
Capture without editor: the selected area goes straight to the strip.
.TP
.B \-\-paste
Paste the set into the active window.
.TP
.B \-\-copy
Copy the set (files and text) to the clipboard.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Show the set strip.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the settings.
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Open the setup check (capture, hotkeys, paste).
.TP
.B \-\-about
Show the version and the authors.
.TP
.B \-\-clear
Clear the set.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Quit the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-\-version
Show the help or the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/markpaste/markpaste.conf
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/markpaste/logs/
The log (events only, no shot contents or comments).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/markpaste/session/
The set kept between restarts, if this is turned on in the settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
